+# Context AI — Syllabus & Exam Assistant
+
+ConnectX Final Project #5: a grounded-RAG study assistant with GPA/study-plan
+tools, a private per-device notebook, flashcards, graded quizzes, and
+multi-turn memory — built on a single tool-calling agent rather than a
+pile of special-cased endpoints.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Grounded syllabus RAG** — FAISS + HuggingFace embeddings over course
+  syllabi (hardcoded samples in `backend/data.py`, plus anything a student
+  adds via pasted text or PDF). `search_syllabus` retrieves with a minimum
+  relevance floor and a per-course cap, so it can actually say "not found"
+  instead of always returning its nearest chunks regardless of quality.
+- **PDF ingestion**, page-aware — `POST /courses/upload` extracts text
+  page-by-page (`backend/pdf_ingest.py`) so citations can point to a real
+  page number (e.g. `CS301 p.4`).
+- **Private per-device notebook** — a student's own PDFs (`POST
+  /notebook/upload`), kept separate from the shared course library and
+  scoped by a client-generated `device_id`. A chat turn can be pinned to
+  just one or more selected notebook docs, which also drops
+  `search_syllabus` from that turn's toolset.
+- **Solutions/answer-key attachment** — a solutions PDF can be attached to
+  either a shared course or a notebook doc (`POST
+  /courses/{code}/solutions`, `POST /notebook/{doc_id}/solutions`),
+  indexed alongside the source material and cited distinctly so the
+  assistant can explain not just the answer but why a given mistake
+  happens.
+- **GPA tools** — `gpa_impact_simulator` (simulate one grade),
+  `gpa_target_planner` (work backward from a goal GPA), and
+  `build_ai_study_plan` (pulls a course's own topic list and exam date
+  straight from its syllabus instead of requiring them retyped;
+  `generate_study_schedule` is still there for an explicit topic list).
+- **Slash commands**, not mode buttons — typing `/` opens a suggestion
+  palette. `/depth` (deeper, longer explanation for this message), `/exam`
+  (frame this message in exam-prep mode), `/flashcards` (10-card deck,
+  topic inferred from the conversation), `/quiz` (5-question graded
+  multiple-choice quiz, same topic inference), `/retry` (a follow-up quiz
+  targeting whatever you've actually gotten wrong so far — not inferred
+  from free-form chat, drawn from real recorded quiz results).
+- **Streaming** (`POST /chat/stream`, SSE) with mid-stream cancellation;
+  `POST /chat` (non-streaming) is also still there.
+- **Multi-turn memory per session**, trimmed to a bounded window of recent
+  turns so a long-running conversation doesn't grow the prompt forever
+  (see Production readiness below).
 
