+## What's stubbed vs. real
+
+- **The 3 sample syllabi are hardcoded** in `backend/data.py` — real
+  ingestion exists for everything added on top via pasted text or PDF.
+  `.docx` isn't handled, only PDF.
+- **Sessions and quiz history are in-memory**, not persisted to a
+  database — they survive a long demo via the TTL sweep (Production
+  readiness above) but are gone on restart. Swapping in Redis or a small
+  SQLite table would make them durable; Postgres + pgvector is the
+  planned direction for the vector store too.
+- **No real accounts** — `session_id` and `device_id` are random ids
+  generated per browser; `DEMO_MODE`'s admin token protects shared
+  writes, but there's no per-user login anywhere.
+- **No automated test suite** — every patch in this project has been
+  verified by hand (unit tests, integration tests, and live browser runs
+  written per change, plus a clean-room apply-and-diff against a fresh
+  clone before delivery) rather than a checked-in `pytest` suite.
 
